      nanos: 39529291
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Pok\303\251Quest Authenticity**\n\nI\'m immersing myself in the Pok\303\251mon universe to ensure Pok\303\251Quest feels genuine. I\'m focusing on the Pok\303\251dex design \342\200\223 clean lines, official colors, and using real PokeAPI sprite URLs for visual consistency. It\'s about capturing that iconic look and feel.\n\n\n**Analyzing Feature Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously breaking down the requested features, particularly focusing on onboarding and the official type system. I\'m ensuring the starter Pok\303\251mon have accurate PokeAPI data and sprites, starting at level 5. I\'ve also outlined the initial trainer profile setup, including name, avatar, and starting resources. I\'m now delving into implementing the official type system with their correct colors.\n\n\n**Mapping Quest Categories**\n\nI\'m now mapping out the tasks/quests system and their connection to the Pok\303\251mon type system for bonus XP. \"Cocina\" maps to Fire, \"Fregar/Lavar\" to Water, and so on. I\'m focusing on balancing the XP and Gold rewards across difficulty levels, from F\303\241cil to Legendaria. I\'ve also implemented the option for XP allocation to active Pok\303\251mon. I am implementing a combo/streak multiplier that rewards streaks with increased XP/Gold gains.\n\n\n**Developing Encounter Mechanics**\n\nI\'ve just added a Pok\303\251mon encounter chance upon task completion, ranging from 12-15%. This triggers a wild capture screen with a Pokeball throwing minigame. I\'ve also implemented a \"Pok\303\251Ball misteriosa\" system for surprise loot like extra gold, potions, or rare candy. I\'m also planning boss battles linked to specific tasks, such as \"Deep Cleaning the Storage Room\" or \"Organizing the Closet.\"\n\n\n**Implementing Exam Features**\n\nI\'m now building out an exam system with integrated countdowns tied to specific tasks; I envision Pomodoro sessions dealing damage to a gym boss. Upon successful exam approval, I plan to award subject badges and significant rewards. I\'m also recording trimester grades for a cumulative average with associated academic achievements.\n\nI\'ve also implemented a study streak counter!\n\nI\'m working on party management and Pok\303\251mon details. The Pok\303\251mon will have detailed status cards including HP bars, Nature, and evolution info. Healing items like Potions and Rare Candies for leveling up will be included. A real evolution chain with animated modals when level requirement is reached (e.g. Charmander Lv 16 -> Charmeleon Lv 36)\n\n\n**Integrating Daily Habits**\n\nI\'m now integrating a daily habits checklist that includes tasks like making the bed and drinking water, along with a Health Connect steps widget to track progress. I\'m focusing on the integration of a step sync simulation, which will simulate the step increment or allow for manual input. Steps will translate to XP and Gold, especially rewarding Flying and Normal types with extra XP, and will feed into the Fitness stat within the Skill Tree. This also includes a progress bar with bonus gold for achieving 100% completion, as well as an animated streak flame.\n\n\n**Expanding Stat Visualization**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the stat radar and progress bars. I\'m visualizing levels, milestones, and unlockable bonuses to create an engaging experience. I\'m also now implementing stat-based unlocks like shop discounts and XP boosts based on steps to enhance the user experience.\n\n\n\n**Defining Item Rewards**\n\nI\'m solidifying the in-game shop\'s items and their functionality. I\'m assigning specific gold values to healing items like Potions and Rare Candies for immediate level-ups. I\'m also confirming the item rarity with the Pok\303\251ball set for wild encounters. I\'m now adding a step-based egg incubator with animated progress for eggs, but legendaries/mythicals will be earned through heroic accomplishments.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Legendary Unlockables**\n\nI\'m currently solidifying the unlock conditions for legendary Pok\303\251mon. I\'m assigning specific tasks: Suicune requires 14 consecutive days of healthy habits and water consumption, Lugia needs 30 unique Pok\303\251mon captures, Ho-Oh demands leveling three Pok\303\251mon to Level 50, and Rayquaza unlocks upon reaching 100,000 total steps. Each will have locked silhouettes with progress bars and celebratory modals. I\'m also planning the inclusion of an epic chiptune fanfare with confetti.\n\n\n**Structuring Project Files**\n\nI\'m now deep in planning the file structure for the app, creating modular components. I\'ve outlined key TypeScript types and data files for Pok\303\251mon, tasks, daily habits, shop items, and more, including a PokeAPI client with local caching. I\'m focusing on audio integration with 8-bit sound synthesizers. The goal is to build a robust, organized foundation.\n\n\n**Organizing App Structure**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the core components and pages, with particular attention to bottom bar navigation with active tabs for a comprehensive user experience: Dashboard, Quests, Study Hub, Team & PC, Daily Tracker, Pok\303\251dex, Shop & Eggs, Legendary Achievements, and Android Studio code. I\'m focusing on their respective functionalities, like the Dashboard\'s overview and step widget, and the Team/PC\'s detailed Pok\303\251mon management.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 725691002
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
