  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Mobile Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the mobile polish and sound integration needed. Specifically, I\'m examining the audio system in `src/utils/audio.ts`. I\'m getting excited, thinking that I could build a comprehensive procedural Chiptune Music Generator + Sound FX library. Next, I need to plan this out.\n\n\n**Planning Music Strategy**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out potential chiptune background music tracks. I envision different tracks with distinct moods and functions. The \"Route 1\" track will be catchy for the home screen, while the \"Pokemon Center\" piece is designed for relaxation in the Party/PC. \"Cycling Road\" will have a driving tempo for habits and health. I am also planning the other tracks, and their uses.\n\n\n**Defining Sound Features**\n\nI am now enumerating all the sound effects. I want the audio engine to have distinct functions: `soundFx.playClick()`, `soundFx.playSelect()`, etc. I\'m also considering background music control and features: `musicEngine.playTrack(trackName)`, muting, and volume controls. I need to make the audio controls really cool, so I want an audio controls widget, including: play/pause, track selection, volume slider, visual equalizer, and auto-change option.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 472004943
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
