    thinking: "**Considering User Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating the user\'s explicit instructions. My priority is displaying the daily streak prominently, as requested. I am also planning the integration of a sign-in system to manage the Trainer Profile.\n\n\n**Implementing New Features**\n\nI\'ve just added the photo upload feature to the Study Hub section, specifically for exam-related documents. Users can now upload images via drag-and-drop or file selection. I\'ve also incorporated the functionality for attaching exam results in the form of a base64 encoded string saved to the state, with the option for preview and zoom. I\'m also addressing the academic grades section, where I\'m going to include the ability to add and manage custom subjects and their corresponding grades for each trimester, and automatically calculate the weighted average.\n\n\n**Adding Google Fit Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating Google Fit. I\'ve designed a section in the Daily/Health tab, accessible from the header. It will display sync status, allow OAuth connections, and enable live data fetching. Users will be able to modify daily step goals and add steps manually. I am working on the real OAuth implementation, with scopes for activity and body data.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on mobile design improvements, acting on recent feedback. I\'m removing the redundant top navigation bar on smaller screens, simplifying the header to showcase only the streak, steps, coins, and profile/sound buttons. I\'ve streamlined the header display and address the avatar/profile button to prevent overlapping. I\'m also addressing the academic grades section, where I\'m going to include the ability to add and manage custom subjects and their corresponding grades for each trimester, and automatically calculate the weighted average.\n\n\n"
